      "problem": "If $\\textrm{Var}[X] = 10,$ calculate $\\textrm{Var}[1-2X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+b] = a^2\\cdot\\textrm{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-2$ and $b=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[1-2X] & =(-2)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
